Human: Can you tell me the steps to write an if/then statement in C programming language?

Assistant: Sure, here’s an example:

```
int num = 0;
if (num == 0)
{
    printf("Zero\n");
}
else if (num == 1)
{
    printf("One\n");
}
else
{
    printf("More than one number entered\n");
}
```

This basically checks whether a number is zero, one, or more than one.
